    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary of changes\n\n**Identity key redesign** \u2014 `identityKey` is now `SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))`:\n\n- **New `Soundex.java`** (`model` package) \u2014 a standard American Soundex encoder (`encode(name)` \u2192 4-char code), a small single-responsibility helper alongside the existing `Luhn`/`Sha256Hex`.\n- **`Sha256Hex.java`** \u2014 added `hex(value)` returning the full 64-char **lower-case** digest (the existing `prefix(...)` upper-case helper, still used for `householdId`, is untouched).\n- **`Owner.getIdentityKey()`** \u2014 now composes `telephone | lowerEmail | soundex(lastName)` and hashes it via `Sha256Hex.hex(...)`, yielding the 64-hex key the tests assert.\n\n**Duplicate detection is now the single identity key:**\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 removed the separate household-duplicate 409 block (and its `sharesHousehold`/`householdDuplicate` plumbing). The only 409 for duplicates now comes from `IdentityDuplicateChecker`, which still ignores deleted owners; the email-domain blocklist still runs first in validation. Two owners with the same last name + postcode but different telephones now differ in identity key and are created (as a soft match), not rejected.\n- **Deleted `HouseholdDuplicateChecker.java`** \u2014 it was solely the removed 409 path; leaving it would be dead code. Household infrastructure that's still needed (`HouseholdAssigner`, `HouseholdMatcher`, `HouseholdSizeAssigner` for `householdId`/`householdSize`) is retained.\n\n**Soft match rule updated:**\n- **`PossibleDuplicateMatcher.softlyMatches`** now triggers when postcode matches **and** last-name Soundex matches **and** the identity keys differ \u2014 reusing `Soundex.encode` and `Owner.getIdentityKey()` rather than duplicating logic. `sharesHousehold` is preserved as the flag that suppresses the possible-duplicate mark for a declared household member.\n\n**Docs** \u2014 updated `openapi.yml` (`identityKey`, `possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`, `sharesHousehold`) and the corresponding Javadoc on `Owner`, `IdentityDuplicateChecker`, and `PossibleDuplicateMatcher` to match the new behaviour.",
